# krew: opt-in — the board roll. NO TIMER (the User 2026-09-17: "standing board it is"): the board no longer rolls daily,
# kanban-day-close archives closed work instead. This unit stays for one deliberate migration by hand, and its
# ExecCondition still refuses a board with open cards (krew-board-roll-ready.py, exit 1 = skipped, not failed: the carry
# re-mints open cards and 30 of 33 respawned at the last roll). The roll command itself (/usr/local/bin/krew-board-roll,
# the board carry) is the install's own and is not shipped here.
[Unit]
Description=krew-board-roll — make today's dated Daily the fleet's current board, carry open cards

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecCondition=/usr/bin/python3 %h/.krew/crew/scripts/krew-crew-run krew-board-roll-ready.py
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c '/usr/local/bin/krew-board-roll >> %h/.hermes/logs/krew-board-roll.log 2>&1'
